[Music]  for fans of matt groening's sci-fi  comedy futurama it may seem like a  millennium has come and gone since we  last saw the planet express crew in  action it's hard to believe that a full  22 years have passed since the show made  its auspicious premiere on fox and that  it's been eight years since its  bittersweet finale brought it to a close  the series fractured runs so it earn a  handful of emmys score a fiercely  devoted fan base and make a legitimate  case for being one of the best animated  series of all time regardless the show  constantly struggled with ratings and  was cancelled by fox after four glorious  seasons only to be reborn on comedy  central with the restructured  direct-to-video films then unfortunately  it was cancelled again after an  additional two seasons low ratings and  cancellations aside every step of the  way graining and company consistently  made futurama that rarest of animated  series one that could easily make you  laugh out loud or openly weep into the  cosmos the show's blend of low brow  humor high-minded insight and raw  unabashed emotion is what helped make  futurama a cult hit in its initial run  on fox it's also a big reason the series  storied legacy only grew in syndication  which ultimately led to its revival on  comedy central and it's why even after  that unexpected gift of a 60-plus  episode revival futurama fans still  clamor for even more cosmic adventures  with the planet express gang we can't  say for sure whether or not another  season of futurama might eventually be  on the horizon though with each passing  day the prospect of new episodes full of  humor heart and random pop culture  references seems about as likely as  ridding yourself of a brain slug of your  own free will  hopes  deleted the only ray of optimism we can  offer is that the cast sounds excited to  get back in the spaceship voice actor  maurice lamarche told sci-fi wire that  the old cast remains in touch and that  they're all ready and willing to head  back to the recording booth should more  episodes arise he went on to say i have  to leave it up to the powers that be but  i know everybody's into it including the  cast so hopefully someday there will be  a futurama reboot but we're well  practiced at the reboot thing since the  cast is willing and now that disney  acquired 20th century studios perhaps  they will want to revive the show seeing  how it still has a fervent fan base  stranger things have happened especially  in the world of futurama guess this is  your lucky day pimperoo  however some longtime viewers have  wondered whether we actually need new  episodes of futurama those fans point  out that all good things do eventually  come to an end and many of the best  things come to an end a little quicker  than most that's especially true of  television thanks to poor ratings some  brilliant shows with amazing potential  became history way too soon and then  there are others that stay on the air  many years past their prime  i know what you mean  either way most fans agree that futurama  ended exactly the way it should have  back in 2013. that's due to the fact  that comedy central's brass did  something fox didn't do so many years  ago they gave the show's creators a  heads up that the end was near that  inside info allowed the futurama team to  ensure that the series received a  fitting swan song one that tugged on the  heartstrings as much as it tickled the  funny bone  quit touching my junk pervert  the show's finale simply titled  meanwhile more than achieved that goal  graining and company imbued the episode  with all the wit wonder and insight  you'd expect from the series icing the  cake with a ravishingly romantic  storyline rarely seen in the annals of  animated television as many have pointed  out new futurama episodes might seem  extraneous in the wake of that finale  not just because meanwhile was such an  effective series end but also because  fond farewells are so rare in an era  where network and streaming executives  always seem to have their axes at the  ready after all one of the key narrative  threads throughout the show's largely  remarkable 140 episode run was that time  is finite no matter how many time  shifting devices or bizarre scenarios  you encounter it's important to  appreciate what you have while you still  have it no it isn't shut your filthy  clam  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite tv shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

